    "usage.heading": "How to use the tools",
    "usage.unit-price.title": "Unit Price Calculator — how to use it",
    "usage.unit-price.body": "Standing in a store wondering whether the 500 g detergent or the 1.2 kg one is the better deal? Enter each product's price and size, and the calculator converts both to a price per 100 g so you can compare instantly. For bundles like \"buy two, get one free\", enter the number of items in the bundle and it computes the true price for the total volume. No sign-up, no install — and your numbers never leave your browser.",
    "usage.char-count.title": "Character Counter — how to use it",
    "usage.char-count.body": "Writing against a character limit — a cover letter, an essay, a social post, or a meta description? Paste your text and you instantly see counts with and without spaces, plus how much room is left against your target. It also shows byte counts (UTF-8 and EUC-KR) for systems that limit by bytes rather than characters. Everything is calculated inside your browser; nothing is sent to a server, so sensitive text is safe to paste.",
    "others.heading": "More from the makers",
    "others.lede": "Other services run by the team behind Toolhub.",
    "others.sta.desc": "Social trend analytics platform for creators and influencers",
    "others.isitai.name": "Is It AI? (isitai.me)",
    "others.isitai.desc": "Free check for whether an image or video was AI-generated",
    "faq.heading": "Frequently asked questions",
    "faq.q1": "What is Toolhub?",
    "faq.a1": "Toolhub is a collection of free online tools — like the unit price calculator — for everyday tasks. There is nothing to install and no account to create: open your browser and it just works. Each tool is built to solve one problem, fast.",
    "faq.q2": "Are all the tools free?",
    "faq.a2": "Yes. Every tool listed on Toolhub is completely free — no payments, no subscriptions. If a paid feature ever appears, it will be clearly labeled on the tool's page.",
    "faq.q3": "Is my data sent to a server?",
    "faq.a3": "No. Toolhub tools are pure static pages: your input is processed entirely inside your browser and never transmitted. Convenience settings such as theme or language are stored only in this browser's localStorage.",
    "faq.q4": "How often are new tools added?",
    "faq.a4": "New tools and improvements are published when they are ready. This directory lists the available tools; there is no fixed weekly release schedule.",
    "footer.privacy": "Privacy Policy",
    "footer.more": "More tools",
    "footer.credit": "Created by rayv",
    "footer.coffee": "☕ Buy me a coffee",
    "why.heading": "Why Toolhub",
    "why.free.title": "No sign-up, always free",
    "why.free.body": "Every tool is completely free and works without an account. Just open it and start — no installs, no subscriptions, no hidden fees.",
    "why.private.title": "Runs in your browser",
    "why.private.body": "All the work happens on your own device. Whatever you type is processed inside your browser and never leaves it, so your data stays private.",
    "why.maintained.title": "Maintained weekly",
    "why.maintained.body": "Each tool launches only after passing a QA checklist, and the whole collection is reviewed every week so calculations stay correct and links keep working.",
